AudD  ·  profile default
                 │ Help › Exit codes
 1 Recognize     │  Getting started  Guide  Commands  Keys >Exit codes< Links 
 2 Now playing   │ Exit codes
 3 Streams       │   0    ok           success, including no match
 4 Recognitions  │   1    unexpected   unexpected error, or no match with --fail-on-no-match
 5 Account       │   2    usage        invalid arguments or input, or a missing tool such as ffmpeg
 6 Settings      │   3    auth         missing or rejected API token, or sign-in needed (audd login)
*7 Help          >   4    quota        quota, plan, or feature not available on the account
                 │   5    network      network or server error; retrying may help
                 │   6    safety       a bound is missing (--limit, --max-files), a confirmation is needed (--yes),
                 │                     --max-requests was reached, or an unfinished job for the same files needs
                 │                     --resume or --new
                 │   7    partial      a batch finished with some files failed
                 │   8    threshold    usage --check found fewer remaining requests than --min-remaining
                 │   130  interrupted  stopped with Ctrl-C; a batch keeps finished files (audd jobs resume continues it)
                 │ 
                 │ Output for scripts
                 │ Piped output is JSON (one document, or JSON lines for streaming commands); --format picks table,
                 │ json, jsonl, or csv. Errors go to stderr as {"error":{"code","message","hint","retryable"}}. audd
                 │ commands --json describes every command.
                 │ 
                 │ api_response
                 │   {"schema_version":1, ...the fields of the API's JSON response}: the response as AudD sent it, with
                 │   "schema_version" added
                 │ 
                 │ commands
                 │   this reference
                 │ 
                 │ docs
                 │   The page's markdown as is, piped or not; with --format json,
                 │   {"schema_version":1,"topic","source","markdown"}. Without a topic, the list of topics
                 │ 
                 │ error
                 │   printed to stderr when a command fails in a machine format
